    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_Task_CommunicateUnresolvedIssues__EndEvent_NursingAdmissionComplete" sourceRef="Task_CommunicateUnresolvedIssues" targetRef="EndEvent_NursingAdmissionComplete"/>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Ann_Task_SendAdmissionEmail">
      <bpmn:text>This email is sent to security, nurse managers, nurse coordinators, Pharmacy, Psychology, Social Work, Supply, Medical Records, the admitting Physician, and other established operational recipients. The email identifies the consumer, county, expected arrival time, assigned unit, assigned Physician, and order-to-treat status and includes the available consumer information attachment.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Task_SendAdmissionEmail" sourceRef="Task_SendAdmissionEmail" targetRef="Ann_Task_SendAdmissionEmail"/>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Ann_Task_PrintNursingAdmitPack">
      <bpmn:text>Print the Nursing Admit Pack on the confirmed admission day rather than solely in response to the advance email because admission dates and arrival times may change. The interview established no required email subject-line format or threading convention.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Task_PrintNursingAdmitPack" sourceRef="Task_PrintNursingAdmitPack" targetRef="Ann_Task_PrintNursingAdmitPack"/>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Ann_Task_ContactPhysicianForEncounter">
      <bpmn:text>The Social Worker may arrange the telemedicine session when the Physician is remote.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Task_ContactPhysicianForEncounter" sourceRef="Task_ContactPhysicianForEncounter" targetRef="Ann_Task_ContactPhysicianForEncounter"/>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Ann_Task_CompleteMedicationReconciliation">
      <bpmn:text>Medication history may come from the Physician, Consumer, originating jail, legal documentation, legal records, or other available records. Nurses do not enter an unverified medication as established fact when the information cannot be confirmed.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Task_CompleteMedicationReconciliation" sourceRef="Task_CompleteMedicationReconciliation" targetRef="Ann_Task_CompleteMedicationReconciliation"/>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Ann_Task_ConsumerSignsConsent">
      <bpmn:text>The Consumer may refuse the consent documents. The informational materials provided by the Mental Health Technician are distinct from consent documents and are provided for consumer information. The Consent for Treatment with Psychoactive Medication requires coordination with the Physician.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Task_ConsumerSignsConsent" sourceRef="Task_ConsumerSignsConsent" targetRef="Ann_Task_ConsumerSignsConsent"/>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Ann_Task_VerifyAdmissionCompletion">
      <bpmn:text>The interview described completion before the 7:00 p.m. shift change as normal operational practice, not as a formally cited regulatory SLA. Routine admissions are expected to be completed before the 7:00 p.m. shift change</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Task_VerifyAdmissionCompletion" sourceRef="Task_VerifyAdmissionCompletion" targetRef="Ann_Task_VerifyAdmissionCompletion"/>
    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="Ann_Task_CommunicateUnresolvedIssues">
      <bpmn:text>This may include clinical, medication, behavioral, or support issues to the Physician, Social Worker, or other responsible treatment staff for continued action.</bpmn:text>
    </bpmn:textAnnotation>
    <bpmn:association id="Assoc_Task_CommunicateUnresolvedIssues" sourceRef="Task_CommunicateUnresolvedIssues" targetRef="Ann_Task_CommunicateUnresolvedIssues"/>
  </bpmn:process>
